IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa3-part8-members.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 8 (A company's members), Chapter 1 (the members of a
-- company) and the first half of Chapter 2 (the register of members, required information, the duties of members,
-- the index): ss 112, 112A, 113 to 113J, lines 1414-1531 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. No seat here; coa3-seat.l4 asks the questions from the seat.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes to the case.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: a "means" definition, an "if"/"where"/"in the case of"/"so long as"/
--               "unless"/"until" condition that fails, a period the text fixes that has run, a flat negative.
--               Each such branch carries  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: list not closed, "includes", undefined term, silent, points outside the
--               sources, or a grant or duty limited by its own wording ("without", "who", "having") and the case is
--               outside the limit. Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- SEAMS taken as INPUTS (PLAN.md section 4): s 1(1) the body is a company; s 853E(6) the market is a relevant market;
-- s 1121 the officer is in default. Each is a MAYBE BOOLEAN: NOTHING passes through as NOTHING.
-- Periods: the Act does not say how "the period of two months beginning with a date" is counted; see NOTES.md fork F3.
-- This module follows the target `main` (1.6.110): no section GIVEN, no REFUSE, no sets, no YMD, `Date day month year`.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Acts a regulative rule in this module can name (the parties are the core's `Party`)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 112 act under Chapters 1 and 2 of Part 8` IS ONE OF
    `s 113(1) the company keeps a register of its members`
    `s 113D(1) the new member provides the required information`
    `s 113E(1) the member gives notice of the change in the required information`
    `s 113J(2) the company alters the index of members' names`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- PART 8, CHAPTER 1: THE MEMBERS OF A COMPANY (s 112)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- gloss: a "subscriber of the memorandum" is one of the people who signed the company's founding document.
-- src:1416 | 112 The members of a company
-- src:1417 | (1) The subscribers of a company's memorandum are deemed to have agreed to become members of the company, and on its registration become members and must be entered as such in its register of members.
@ref s 112(1) The members of a company (src:1416-1417)
GIVEN `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(1) the subscriber is deemed to have agreed to become a member of the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The subscribers of a company's memorandum"

@ref s 112(1) The members of a company (src:1417)
GIVEN `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(1) the subscriber becomes a member of the company on its registration` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The subscribers of a company's memorandum"
    ELSE IF `the company has been registered`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on its registration become members" ("upon" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))

@ref s 112(1) The members of a company (src:1417)
GIVEN `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(1) the subscriber must be entered as a member in the register of members` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The subscribers of a company's memorandum"
    ELSE IF `the company has been registered`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on its registration become members and must be entered as such"

-- src:1418 | (2) Every other person who agrees to become a member of a company, and whose name is entered in its register of members, is a member of the company.
@ref s 112(2) Every other person who agrees to become a member (src:1418)
GIVEN `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person agrees to become a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's name is entered in the company's register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(2) the person is a member of the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every other person" (a subscriber is dealt with by s 112(1))
    ELSE IF `the person agrees to become a member of the company` AND `the person's name is entered in the company's register of members`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every other person who agrees to become a member of a company, and whose name is entered in its register of members, is a member" (a sufficient condition; no "only")

-- The answer the rest of the Act asks for ("member" in the Companies Acts, PLAN section 4.2: `s 112 the person is a member of the company`).
-- src:1417 | (1) The subscribers of a company's memorandum are deemed to have agreed to become members of the company, and on its registration become members and must be entered as such in its register of members.
-- src:1418 | (2) Every other person who agrees to become a member of a company, and whose name is entered in its register of members, is a member of the company.
@ref s 112(1)-(2) The members of a company (src:1417-1418)
GIVEN `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person agrees to become a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's name is entered in the company's register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112 the person is a member of the company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum`
    THEN `s 112(1) the subscriber becomes a member of the company on its registration` `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum` `the company has been registered`
    ELSE `s 112(2) the person is a member of the company` `the person is a subscriber of the company's memorandum` `the person agrees to become a member of the company` `the person's name is entered in the company's register of members`

-- s 112(3) is blank in this text (a row of dots): coverage row `repealed or blank in this text`.

-- src:1420 | (4) Where an individual’s name is entered in a company’s register of members but is not in the form required by section 113A, that does not affect the person becoming a member of the company by virtue of subsection (2).
@ref s 112(4) The form of an individual's name (src:1420)
GIVEN `the person agrees to become a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an individual's name is entered in the company's register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is in the form required by section 113A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(4) the person becomes a member under s 112(2) although the entered name is not in the form required by s 113A` MEANS
    IF NOT (`an individual's name is entered in the company's register of members` AND NOT `the name is in the form required by section 113A`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an individual’s name is entered in a company’s register of members but is not in the form required by section 113A" (the "where" does not hold, so s 112(4) does not apply)
    ELSE IF `the person agrees to become a member of the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 112(4) preserves membership "by virtue of subsection (2)", which also needs the person to agree to become a member

-- =========================================================================================================
-- PART 8, CHAPTER 2: REGISTER OF MEMBERS (ss 112A, 113 to 113J)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- s 112A is blank in this text (a row of dots): coverage row `repealed or blank in this text`.

-- ---- s 113(1): the duty to keep a register -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1425 | 113 Register of members
-- src:1426 | (1) Every company must keep a register of its members.
@ref s 113(1) Register of members (src:1425-1426)
GIVEN `s 1(1) the body is a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(1) the company must keep a register of its members` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1(1) the body is a company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1(1) "unless the context otherwise requires"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The Company is the named party; the text fixes no time, so the rule has no WITHIN.
@ref s 113(1) Register of members (src:1426)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 112 act under Chapters 1 and 2 of Part 8`
`s 113(1) the company must keep a register of its members (duty)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 113(1) the company keeps a register of its members`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not keep a register of its members"

-- ---- s 113(2) and (2A): what must be entered. THE TEXT SHOWS TWO VERSIONS OF s 113(2) (fork F1, NOTES.md) ----

-- src:1427 | (2) There must be entered in the register—
-- src:1428 | (a) the names and addresses of the members,
-- src:1429 | (b) the date on which each person was registered as a member, and
-- src:1430 | (c) the date at which any person ceased to be a member.
-- src:1431 | (2) There must be entered in the register, in respect of each person who is a member—
-- src:1432 | (a) the required information (see sections 113A and 113B), and
-- src:1433 | (b) the date on which the person was registered as a member.
-- src:1434 | (2A) Where a person ceases to be a member there must be entered in the register the date at which the person’s membership ceased.
@ref s 113(2) and (2A) Entries in the register of members (both versions of s 113(2) as the text shows them) (src:1427-1434)
DECLARE `s 113(2) entry in the register of members` IS ONE OF
    `s 113(2)(a) the names and addresses of the members`
    `s 113(2)(a) the required information about each member`
    `s 113(2)(b) the date on which the person was registered as a member`
    `s 113(2)(c) the date at which any person ceased to be a member`
    `s 113(2) some other entry`

-- gloss: the first version of s 113(2) lists three entries: names and addresses, the date of registration, the date of ceasing.
-- src:1427 | (2) There must be entered in the register—
-- src:1428 | (a) the names and addresses of the members,
-- src:1429 | (b) the date on which each person was registered as a member, and
-- src:1430 | (c) the date at which any person ceased to be a member.
@ref s 113(2) There must be entered in the register (first version in the text) (src:1427-1430)
GIVEN entry IS A `s 113(2) entry in the register of members`
      `the entry is in respect of a person who is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(2) (first version) the register must contain the entry` MEANS
    IF NOT `the entry is in respect of a person who is a member`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the names and addresses of the members", "each person ... a member"
    ELSE CONSIDER entry
         WHEN `s 113(2)(a) the names and addresses of the members` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 113(2)(b) the date on which the person was registered as a member` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 113(2)(c) the date at which any person ceased to be a member` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 113(2)(a) the required information about each member` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the first version names "the names and addresses of the members", not "the required information"
         WHEN `s 113(2) some other entry` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): other subsections of s 113 require other entries

-- gloss: the second version says "the required information" (names or titles and service addresses, ss 113A and 113B) instead of names and addresses.
-- src:1431 | (2) There must be entered in the register, in respect of each person who is a member—
-- src:1432 | (a) the required information (see sections 113A and 113B), and
-- src:1433 | (b) the date on which the person was registered as a member.
@ref s 113(2) There must be entered in the register, in respect of each person who is a member (second version in the text) (src:1431-1433)
GIVEN entry IS A `s 113(2) entry in the register of members`
      `the entry is in respect of a person who is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(2) (second version) the register must contain the entry` MEANS
    IF NOT `the entry is in respect of a person who is a member`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of each person who is a member"
    ELSE CONSIDER entry
         WHEN `s 113(2)(a) the required information about each member` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 113(2)(b) the date on which the person was registered as a member` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 113(2)(a) the names and addresses of the members` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the second version says "the required information" (see ss 113A and 113B)
         WHEN `s 113(2)(c) the date at which any person ceased to be a member` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the second version deals with ceasing in s 113(2A)
         WHEN `s 113(2) some other entry` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): other subsections of s 113 require other entries

-- src:1434 | (2A) Where a person ceases to be a member there must be entered in the register the date at which the person’s membership ceased.
@ref s 113(2A) Where a person ceases to be a member (src:1434)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(2A) the register must contain the date at which the person's membership ceased` MEANS
    IF `the person has ceased to be a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person ceases to be a member"

-- ---- s 113(3) to (6): the further entries -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1435 | (3) In the case of a company having a share capital, there must be entered in the register , with the names and addresses of the members, a statement of—
-- src:1436 | (a) the shares held by each member, distinguishing each share—
-- src:1437 | (i) by its number (so long as the share has a number), and
-- src:1438 | (ii) where the company has more than one class of issued shares, by its class, and
-- src:1439 | (b) the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member.
@ref s 113(3) Companies having a share capital (src:1435-1439)
