GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share has a number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(3)(a)(i) the register must distinguish the share by its number` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has a share capital`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a company having a share capital"
    ELSE IF `the share has a number`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(so long as the share has a number)"

@ref s 113(3)(a)(ii) Distinguishing each share by its class (src:1436-1438)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has more than one class of issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(3)(a)(ii) the register must distinguish the share by its class` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has a share capital`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a company having a share capital"
    ELSE IF `the company has more than one class of issued shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the company has more than one class of issued shares"

@ref s 113(3)(b) The amount paid on the shares (src:1439)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(3)(b) the register must state the amount paid or agreed to be considered as paid on the shares of each member` MEANS
    IF `the company has a share capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a company having a share capital"

-- src:1440 | (4) If the company has converted any of its shares into stock, and given notice of the conversion to the registrar, the register of members must show the amount and class of stock held by each member instead of the amount of shares and the particulars relating to shares specified above.
@ref s 113(4) Conversion of shares into stock (src:1440)
GIVEN `the company has converted any of its shares into stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has given notice of the conversion to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(4) the register must show the amount and class of stock held by each member instead of the amount of shares and the particulars relating to shares` MEANS
    IF `the company has converted any of its shares into stock` AND `the company has given notice of the conversion to the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company has converted any of its shares into stock, and given notice of the conversion to the registrar"

-- src:1441 | (5) In the case of joint holders of shares or stock in a company, the company's register of members must state the names of each joint holder.
-- src:1442 | In other respects joint holders are regarded for the purposes of this Chapter as a single member (so that the register must show a single service address).
@ref s 113(5) Joint holders (src:1441-1442)
GIVEN `there are joint holders of shares or stock in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
