    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of joint holders of shares or stock in a company"

@ref s 113(5) Joint holders (second sentence) (src:1442)
GIVEN `there are joint holders of shares or stock in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(5) joint holders are regarded for the purposes of Chapter 2 as a single member, so that the register must show a single service address` MEANS
    IF `there are joint holders of shares or stock in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In other respects joint holders are regarded for the purposes of this Chapter as a single member" (the "joint holders" case is absent)

-- src:1443 | (6) In the case of a company that does not have a share capital but has more than one class of members, there must be entered in the register , with the names and addresses of the members, a statement of the class to which each member belongs.
@ref s 113(6) Companies without a share capital but with classes of members (src:1443)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has more than one class of members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(6) the register must contain a statement of the class to which each member belongs` MEANS
