    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a company that does not have a share capital but has more than one class of members"

-- ---- s 113(6A) to (6D): old information after a change ------------------------------------------------------
-- The traded or non-traded status is the answer of s 113(9) below, passed in as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.

-- src:1444 | (6A) Where any of the information required to be entered in a company’s register of members changes and, at the time of the change, it is a non-traded company—
-- src:1445 | (a) the fact that the information has changed does not relieve the company from the obligation to include the old information in the register if it has not already done so,
@ref s 113(6A)(a) Old information still to be included (src:1444-1445)
GIVEN `information required to be entered in the register has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 113(9) the company is a non-traded company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the old information has already been included in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(6A)(a) the change does not relieve the company from including the old information in the register` MEANS
    IF NOT `information required to be entered in the register has changed`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any of the information required to be entered in a company’s register of members changes"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 113(9) the company is a non-traded company`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the time of the change, it is a non-traded company"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 853E(6) decides "relevant market"
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the old information has already been included in the register`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it has not already done so"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1444 | (6A) Where any of the information required to be entered in a company’s register of members changes and, at the time of the change, it is a non-traded company—
-- src:1446 | (b) the old information must be retained in the register until its removal is authorised by section 121 or by court order under section 125, and
@ref s 113(6A)(b) Old information to be retained (src:1444 and src:1446)
GIVEN `information required to be entered in the register has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 113(9) the company is a non-traded company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `its removal has been authorised by section 121 or by court order under section 125` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(6A)(b) the old information must be retained in the register` MEANS
    IF NOT `information required to be entered in the register has changed`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any of the information required to be entered in a company’s register of members changes"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 113(9) the company is a non-traded company`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the time of the change, it is a non-traded company"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 853E(6) decides "relevant market"
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `its removal has been authorised by section 121 or by court order under section 125`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until its removal is authorised by section 121 or by court order under section 125"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1444 | (6A) Where any of the information required to be entered in a company’s register of members changes and, at the time of the change, it is a non-traded company—
-- src:1447 | (c) a note must be included in the register recording the date on which the information changed and the date on which the change was entered in the register.
