-- ---- s 113(7) and (8): the offence and its penalty ------------------------------------------------------------
-- THE SHAPE SHARED BY THE OFFENCE SECTIONS OF THIS PART: "an offence is committed by (a) the company, and (b) every
-- officer of the company who is in default". Later offence sections of the same shape (ss 113J(5), 114(5), 115(5),
-- 118(1), 120(3), 120B(1), 123(4), 130(2), 132(3), 135(4)) call this one rule after testing their own condition.
-- The officer limb takes the answer of s 1121 as a MAYBE BOOLEAN (PLAN section 4.2).

-- src:1453 | (7) If , without reasonable excuse, a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:1454 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1455 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 113(7) Offence by the company and its officers in default (src:1453-1455)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with section 113` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the default is without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(7) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has made default in complying with section 113`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If , without reasonable excuse, a company makes default in complying with this section an offence is committed by"
    ELSE IF NOT `the default is without reasonable excuse`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without reasonable excuse" (the excuse sits inside the "if" gate of the offence; fork F35)
         ELSE `s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` person `s 1121 the officer is in default`

@ref s 113(7)(a)-(b) Offence by the company and its officers in default (src:1453-1455)
GIVEN person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(7)(a)-(b) the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN Company THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN Director THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 decides who is "in default"
    WHEN `Company secretary` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 decides who is "in default"
    WHEN `Officer in default` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 decides who is "in default"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and its officers in default and says nothing of any other person

-- src:1456 | (8) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 113(8) Penalty (summary conviction only) (src:1456)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 113(8) the penalty for an offence under s 113` MEANS
    -- "a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine
    -- not exceeding one-tenth of level 3": the pounds a level stands for are set outside the Act.
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- ---- s 113(9): the definitions of "non-traded company", "relevant market" and "traded company" ---------------

-- src:1459 | “relevant market” has the meaning given by section 853E(6);
@ref s 113(9) "relevant market" has the meaning given by section 853E(6) (src:1459)
GIVEN `s 853E(6) the market is a relevant market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(9) the market is a relevant market` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 853E(6) the market is a relevant market`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant market” has the meaning given by section 853E(6)" (the answer is s 853E(6)'s)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 853E(6)

-- src:1460 | “traded company” means a company any of whose shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market or on any other market which is outside the United Kingdom.
@ref s 113(9) "traded company" (src:1460)
GIVEN `any of the company's shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `any of the company's shares are admitted to trading on any other market which is outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(9) the company is a traded company` MEANS
    IF `any of the company's shares are admitted to trading on any other market which is outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `any of the company's shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“traded company” means a company any of whose shares are admitted to trading on a relevant market or on any other market which is outside the United Kingdom"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "relevant market" has the meaning given by section 853E(6)

-- src:1458 | “non-traded company” means a company that is not a traded company;
@ref s 113(9) "non-traded company" (src:1458)
GIVEN `s 113(9) the company is a traded company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(9) the company is a non-traded company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 113(9) the company is a traded company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“non-traded company” means a company that is not a traded company"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "traded company" depends on section 853E(6)

