-- src:1480 | 113D Duty on new members to notify required information
-- src:1481 | (1) A person who becomes a member of a company must provide the company with the required information about the member (see sections 113A and 113B).
-- src:1482 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if or to the extent that—
@ref s 113D(1)-(2) Duty on new members to notify required information (src:1480-1482)
GIVEN `the person has become a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has already provided the required information to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person became a member on the company's incorporation and the information is contained in the application for the registration of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113D(1) the person must provide the company with the required information about the member, subject to s 113D(2)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has become a member of the company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who becomes a member of a company"
    ELSE IF       `the person has already provided the required information to the company`
              OR  `the person became a member on the company's incorporation and the information is contained in the application for the registration of the company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if or to the extent that"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- "the period of N months beginning with a date": the Act does not say how it is counted (fork F3). Read as: the period
-- ends on the day before the date N months later; where that date does not exist in the later month, it ends on the
-- last day of that month. `add months` clamps to the last day of the target month, so a clamped result is the last day.
-- src:1485 | (3) A person must comply with this section within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the person became a member.
@ref s 113D(3) Within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the person became a member (src:1485)
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113D(3) the last day of the period of months beginning with a date` MEANS
    LET `the corresponding date` MEANS `add months` `the first day of the period` months
    IN IF DATE_DAY `the corresponding date` LESS THAN DATE_DAY `the first day of the period`
       THEN `the corresponding date`
       ELSE `the corresponding date` MINUS 1

@ref s 113D(3) Within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the person became a member (src:1485)
GIVEN `the date on which the person became a member` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113D(3) the last day for providing the information` MEANS
    `s 113D(3) the last day of the period of months beginning with a date` `the date on which the person became a member` 2

@ref s 113D(3) Within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the person became a member (src:1485)
GIVEN `the date on which the person became a member` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the person provided the information` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113D(3) the person provided the information within the period of two months` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the person provided the information` LESS THAN `the date on which the person became a member`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 113D(3) counts the period from the day the person became a member; information provided earlier is dealt with by s 113D(2)(a)
    ELSE IF `the date on which the person provided the information` AT MOST `s 113D(3) the last day for providing the information` `the date on which the person became a member`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the person became a member"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the clock counts days from the day the person became a member (day 0).
@ref s 113D(3) Within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the person became a member (src:1485)
GIVEN `the date on which the person became a member` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113D(3) the number of days from becoming a member to the last day for providing the information` MEANS
    `s 113D(3) the last day for providing the information` `the date on which the person became a member` MINUS `the date on which the person became a member`

-- src:1481 | (1) A person who becomes a member of a company must provide the company with the required information about the member (see sections 113A and 113B).
-- src:1485 | (3) A person must comply with this section within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the person became a member.
@ref s 113D(1) and (3) Duty on new members to notify required information (src:1481 and src:1485)
GIVEN `the date on which the person became a member` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 112 act under Chapters 1 and 2 of Part 8`
`s 113D(1) the new member must provide the company with the required information within two months (duty)` MEANS
    PARTY Member
    MUST `s 113D(1) the new member provides the required information`
    WITHIN (`s 113D(3) the number of days from becoming a member to the last day for providing the information` `the date on which the person became a member`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Member BECAUSE "the required information was not provided within two months beginning with the date the person became a member"

-- src:1486 | 113E Duty on member to notify changes to required information
-- src:1487 | (1) A person who is a member of a company must give notice to the company of any change in the required information about the member (see sections 113A and 113B).
