-- src:1488 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the change occurred.
@ref s 113E(2) The notice must specify the date of the change (src:1488)
GIVEN `the member gives notice under section 113E(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113E(2) the notice must specify the date on which the change occurred` MEANS
    IF `the member gives notice under section 113E(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The notice must specify" (the sentence speaks of the notice, and there is none)

-- src:1489 | (3) A person must comply with this section within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the change occurred.
@ref s 113E(3) Within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the change occurred (src:1489)
GIVEN `the date on which the change occurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113E(3) the last day for giving notice of the change` MEANS
    `s 113D(3) the last day of the period of months beginning with a date` `the date on which the change occurred` 2

@ref s 113E(3) Within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the change occurred (src:1489)
GIVEN `the date on which the change occurred` IS A DATE
      `the date on which notice of the change was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113E(3) the member gave notice of the change within the period of two months` MEANS
    IF `the date on which notice of the change was given` LESS THAN `the date on which the change occurred`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 113E(3) counts the period from the day the change occurred; notice given before the change is not mentioned
    ELSE IF `the date on which notice of the change was given` AT MOST `s 113E(3) the last day for giving notice of the change` `the date on which the change occurred`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the change occurred"

@ref s 113E(3) Within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the change occurred (src:1489)
GIVEN `the date on which the change occurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113E(3) the number of days from the change to the last day for giving notice` MEANS
    `s 113E(3) the last day for giving notice of the change` `the date on which the change occurred` MINUS `the date on which the change occurred`

-- src:1487 | (1) A person who is a member of a company must give notice to the company of any change in the required information about the member (see sections 113A and 113B).
-- src:1489 | (3) A person must comply with this section within the period of two months beginning with the date on which the change occurred.
@ref s 113E(1) and (3) Duty on member to notify changes to required information (src:1487 and src:1489)
GIVEN `the date on which the change occurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 112 act under Chapters 1 and 2 of Part 8`
