    IF NOT `an offence under section 113G(1) or (2) is committed by a firm`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is committed by a firm"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the firm who is in default"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 decides who is "in default"

-- "the general limit in a magistrates' court" is not in the Act's own words: s 1131 fixes six months only for an
-- offence committed before 2 May 2022; otherwise the number is outside the sources and is an INPUT here (a Period).
-- src:1497 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:1498 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:1499 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:1500 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or a fine (or both);
-- src:1501 | (ii) in Scotland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both) and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-fifth of the statutory maximum;
-- src:1502 | (iii) in Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both) and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-fifth of the statutory maximum.
@ref s 113G(4) Penalties (src:1497-1502)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court` IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 113G(4) the penalty for an offence under s 113G` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST `the general limit in a magistrates' court`, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 0.2), TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 0.2), TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text distinguishes summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland and in Northern Ireland

-- ---- s 113H: basic false statement offences ---------------------------------------------------------------------

