-- src:1515 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:1516 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:1517 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:1518 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or a fine (or both);
-- src:1519 | (ii) in Scotland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both) and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-fifth of the statutory maximum;
-- src:1520 | (iii) in Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both) and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-fifth of the statutory maximum.
@ref s 113I(4) Penalties (src:1515-1520)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court` IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 113I(4) the penalty for an offence under s 113I` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST `the general limit in a magistrates' court`, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 0.2), TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 0.2), TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text distinguishes summary conviction in England and Wales, in Scotland and in Northern Ireland

-- =========================================================================================================
-- THE INDEX OF MEMBERS (s 113J)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- gloss: an "index of members' names" lets one find a member's entry in the register; a company with 50 members or fewer
-- (or one whose register is itself in the form of an index) need not keep one.
-- src:1522 | 113J Index of members
-- src:1523 | (1) Every company having more than 50 members must keep an index of the names or titles of the members of the company (to be known as “the index of members’ names”), unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index.
@ref s 113J(1) Index of members (src:1522-1523)
GIVEN `the number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113J(1) the company must keep an index of the names or titles of its members` MEANS
    IF `the number of members of the company` AT MOST 50
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every company having more than 50 members"
    ELSE IF `the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the register of members is in such a form as to constitute in itself an index"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1524 | (2) The company must make any necessary alteration in the index within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is made in the register of members.
@ref s 113J(2) Alteration of the index within 14 days (src:1524)
GIVEN `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113J(2) the last day for making the alteration in the index` MEANS
    `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members` PLUS 14 -- "within 14 days after the date": the 14th day after it

@ref s 113J(2) Alteration of the index within 14 days (src:1524)
GIVEN `s 113J(1) the company must keep an index of the names or titles of its members` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the necessary alteration is made in the index` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113J(2) the company made the necessary alteration in the index within 14 days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 113J(1) the company must keep an index of the names or titles of its members`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the date on which the necessary alteration is made in the index` LESS THAN `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 113J(2) counts from the register's alteration; an earlier alteration of the index is not mentioned
        ELSE IF `the date on which the necessary alteration is made in the index` AT MOST `s 113J(2) the last day for making the alteration in the index` `the date on which the alteration is made in the register of members`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date on which any alteration is made in the register of members"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 113J(2) speaks of "the index", which only s 113J(1) requires
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 113J(2) speaks of "the index", which only s 113J(1) requires

@ref s 113J(2) Alteration of the index within 14 days (src:1524)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 112 act under Chapters 1 and 2 of Part 8`
`s 113J(2) the company must alter the index within 14 days after the alteration of the register (duty)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 113J(2) the company alters the index of members' names`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the index was not altered within 14 days after the register was altered"

-- src:1525 | (3) The index must include the same details of a person’s name or title as are entered in the register of members.
